## Model card (verified spec facts only)

- **Name:** MiniMax M3.1 Flash Preview
- **Short description:** MiniMax's latest M-series language model — a frontier multimodal coding model with a 1M context window and tunable thinking depth, for agentic reasoning, tool use, coding, and long-context tasks. Preview tier: M Plan / MiniMax Code only.
- **Provider / access:** MiniMax Platform — Anthropic-compatible `https://api.minimax.io/anthropic` (recommended), OpenAI-compatible `https://api.minimax.io/v1`, OpenAI Responses also supported. Available only through M Plan and MiniMax Code for now (official docs note, 2026-10-01). Not an alias — a distinct M3.1 Flash preview tier.
- **Release / knowledge:** Released 2026-09-27 (curated meta; vendor docs list it as the latest M-series model as of 2026-10-01). Knowledge cutoff: no verified public data found.
- **IDs:** `MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview` (no OpenCode Zen Free ID exists)
- **Context window:** 1,000,000 tokens total (verified via official MiniMax platform docs — Model Invocation table and 1M-token context accordion; max output: no verified public number found)
- **Modalities:** Text, image, and video in; text out; reasoning always on (thinking cannot be disabled — `effort` accepts `low`/`medium`/`high`/`xhigh`/`max`, default `max`); tool calls and structured task execution supported (verified via official docs)
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-01):** No public per-token price — MiniMax M Plan / Token Plan subscription and MiniMax Code only (no Zen Free ID)
- **Architecture:** Architecture details (params, MoE/attention) unpublished for this preview; its M3 sibling uses proprietary MiniMax Sparse Attention (MSA) with 1M context — noted as family context only, not confirmed for this preview. Open-weights status: not published for the preview.

